# utilities/ holds build scripts, crawlers, specs, and other dev-only files.
# Nothing here is part of the site, so every request under it gets a 403.
# Anything pages need at runtime belongs elsewhere (llab/lib, teacher/, ...).
#
# We use mod_alias (RedirectMatch) rather than `Require all denied` because
# it only needs `AllowOverride FileInfo`, which the root .htaccess already
# depends on (Header, AddCharset, ErrorDocument). `Require` needs AuthConfig,
# and if that isn't allowed Apache answers every request here with a 500.
# That would still block access, but it would show up as a server error.
#
# RedirectMatch matches against the decoded, normalized URL path, so `..`
# and %-encoding tricks can't sneak past it.
RedirectMatch 403 "/utilities/"
